>> servings: 6

Set #oven to 150C
Mix together @dark sugar{32%g}, @salt{4.5%g}, @paprika{0.5%tbsp}, @ground cumin{0.5%tsp}, @black pepper{0.5%tsp}, @ground coriander{0.5%tsp}, @ground fennel seeds{0.5%tsp} & @cayenne pepper{pinch} in a bowl.
Take roughly half of the spice mixture and rub it on @pork butt{1.5%kg} covering all sides.
Heat up @vegetable oil{7.5%ml} in a large #dutch oven{} until shimmering.
Brown @pork butt{} on all sides, making sure not to burn the sugar.
In a large bowl mix together @ketchup{112.5%g}, @dark molasses{55%g}, @apple cider vinegar{30%g}, @worcestershire sauce{15%ml}, @liquid smoke{7.5%ml}, @mustart{7.5%ml}, @hot sauce{5%ml}.
Turn off gas burner for the dutch oven and pour in @burboun{120%ml} and light with match. Watch out for tall flames and turn on burner again.
When flames have died add in half of the fluid mixture and save the rest in the fridge with the spice mixture.
Cover dutch oven and place in oven for ~{3%hour}, then uncover and cook for ~{1%hour}.